{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeMXbwU7k9STCm3wfCeGb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019MeFktemaKzRESRJcpPhYP","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/workloads/controllers/job/","prompt":"Extract VERBATIM text (copy exact sentences, do NOT paraphrase, summarize, or rewrite) from these sections of this page. Preserve the original wording word-for-word:\n\n1. The opening definition paragraphs — what a Job creates, what \"run to completion\" means, tracking successful completions, what happens when the Job is deleted, and suspending a Job.\n2. \"Parallel execution for Jobs\" — the three types of jobs (non-parallel, parallel with fixed completion count, parallel with a work queue) and the .spec.completions and .spec.parallelism fields.\n3. \"Handling Pod and container failures\" and \"Pod backoff failure policy\" — especially .spec.backoffLimit and its default value.\n4. \"Job termination and cleanup\" — including activeDeadlineSeconds.\n5. \"TTL mechanism for finished Jobs\" — ttlSecondsAfterFinished.\n6. Any sentence describing the Job's completion state / status.succeeded / when a Job is considered complete.\n7. \"Job patterns\" if present.\n\nOutput as markdown with the section headings, quoting the source text exactly."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5616,"cache_read_input_tokens":87413,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5616},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b489fccf-1e67-4e89-a205-d6eb19382b09","uuid":"9c602a9e-f256-4691-aeee-2ea58f570dfc","timestamp":"2026-08-24T11:54:42.048Z","request_id":"req_011CeMXbvdmCfrwajoo6mcVJ"}
