{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeMXbwU7k9STCm3wfCeGb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DEnhaQX1dXwvq7QL4fD62R","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/workloads/controllers/cron-jobs/","prompt":"Extract VERBATIM text (copy exact sentences, do NOT paraphrase, summarize, or rewrite) from these sections of this page. Preserve the original wording word-for-word:\n\n1. The opening definition paragraphs — what a CronJob creates, that it runs Jobs on a repeating schedule, and the comparison to a crontab line in Unix.\n2. Any caution/warning about CronJobs creating a Job \"about once per execution time\" and jobs being created twice or not at all (idempotency).\n3. \"Cron schedule syntax\" — the full schedule field table/format and any examples, including the note about time zones and .spec.timeZone.\n4. \"Job template\" (.spec.jobTemplate) — the statement that it is the template for a Job and is required.\n5. \"Deadline for delayed Job start\" — startingDeadlineSeconds.\n6. \"Concurrency policy\" — the Allow, Forbid, and Replace values and their definitions.\n7. \"Jobs history limits\" — successfulJobsHistoryLimit and failedJobsHistoryLimit and their defaults.\n8. Any statement about the CronJob controller checking the schedule / how often.\n\nOutput as markdown with the section headings, quoting the source text exactly."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5616,"cache_read_input_tokens":87413,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5616},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b489fccf-1e67-4e89-a205-d6eb19382b09","uuid":"1bca2835-6e48-41ca-863a-15e8a119d8db","timestamp":"2026-08-24T11:54:47.695Z