{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeMXp7jqhtJ4BssvebDuJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01V2qngM44gFH3jiVsJAVDE8","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://kubernetes.io/docs/tasks/run-application/horizontal-pod-autoscale/","prompt":"Extract VERBATIM (exact wording, no paraphrasing) from this HorizontalPodAutoscaler page:\n\n1. The opening definition paragraphs — what a HorizontalPodAutoscaler is, what it automatically updates, the statement that horizontal scaling means deploying more Pods (as opposed to vertical scaling), and what happens when load decreases.\n2. The statement that horizontal pod autoscaling does not apply to objects that can't be scaled (e.g. DaemonSet).\n3. \"How does a HorizontalPodAutoscaler work?\" — the description of it being implemented as a Kubernetes API resource and a controller, the intermittent control loop, and the default interval the controller runs at.\n4. Any sentence naming which workload resources an HPA can target (Deployment, StatefulSet, ReplicaSet).\n\nQuote exactly."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8346,"cache_read_input_tokens":116816,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8346},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b489fccf-1e67-4e89-a205-d6eb19382b09","uuid":"2965aac9-1ced-4d4c-84fa-fd3244559a57","timestamp":"2026-08-24T11:57:09.290Z","request_id":"req_011CeMXp6tEuUTm5xrx45qAt"}
