{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"/docs/concepts/workloads/controllers/replicaset/)\n\n## Purpose\n\nA ReplicaSet's purpose is to maintain a stable set of replica Pods running at any given time. Usually, you define a Deployment and let"}},"session_id":"b489fccf-1e67-4e89-a205-d6eb19382b09","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"b2f7d4ae-96d2-4716-82c5-53f7b37ef513"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" that Deployment manage ReplicaSets automatically.\n\nA ReplicaSet's purpose is to maintain a stable set of replica Pods running at any given time. As such, it is often used to guarantee the availability of a specified number of identical Pods.\n\n## How a ReplicaSet"}},"session_id":"b489fccf-1e67-4e89-a205-d6eb19382b09","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"f5979042-c63c-42c4-8164-846e1a24f31e"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" works\n\nA ReplicaSet is defined with fields, including a selector that specifies how to identify Pods it can acquire, a number of replicas indicating how many Pods it should be maintaining, and a pod template spec"}},"session_id":"b489fccf-1e67-4e89-a205-d6eb19382b09","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"c9bafd5b-c165-4ccb-a5a0-26a5ff0f64c0"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"ifying the data of new Pods it should create to meet the number of replicas criteria. A ReplicaSet then fulfills its purpose by creating and deleting Pods as needed to reach the desired number. When a"}},"session_id":"b489fccf-1e67-4e89-a205-d6eb19382b09","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"fe7b1b61-aa59-4ef4-8b29-2e57e8486ed2"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" ReplicaSet needs to create new Pods, it uses its Pod template.\n\nA ReplicaSet is linked to its Pods via the Pods' `metadata.ownerReferences` field, which specifies what resource the current object is owned by. All"}},"session_id":"b489fccf-1e67-4e89-a205-d6eb19382b09","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"04800d52-d9e3-44b8-bacd-9b3b2cde32f1"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" Pods acquired by a ReplicaSet have their owning ReplicaSet's identifying information within their ownerReferences field. It's through this link that the ReplicaSet knows of the state of the Pods it is maintaining and plans accordingly.\n\nA ReplicaSet ident"}},"session_id":"b489fccf-1e67-4e89-a205-d6eb19382b09","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"1216832e-fde4-42bd-9e54-4f4bfdf71ad2"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"ifies new Pods to acquire by using its selector. If there is a Pod that has no OwnerReference or the OwnerReference is not a Controller and it matches a ReplicaSet's selector, it will be immediately acquired by said"}},"session_id":"b489fccf-1e67-4e89-a205-d6eb19382b09","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"9043cc7c-81d1-40ff-b1cf-707a81ba3aaa"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" ReplicaSet.\n\n## When to use a ReplicaSet\n\nA ReplicaSet ensures that a specified number of pod replicas are running at any given time. However, a Deployment is a higher-level concept that manages ReplicaSets"}},"session_id":"b489fccf-1e67-4e89-a205-d6eb19382b09","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"7bb2629b-08de-4766-8980-f7b36cc2285f"}
