{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"ires manual intervention to repair.\n\n## Pod Identity\n\nStatefulSet Pods have a unique identity that consists of an ordinal, a stable network identity, and stable storage. The identity sticks to the Pod, regardless of which node it's ("}},"session_id":"b489fccf-1e67-4e89-a205-d6eb19382b09","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"12ba490d-9ccc-4c03-9c9e-a53e14204d32"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"re)scheduled on.\n\n### Ordinal Index\n\nFor a StatefulSet with N replicas, each Pod in the StatefulSet will be assigned an integer ordinal, that is unique over the Set. By default, pods will be assigned ordinals from 0 up"}},"session_id":"b489fccf-1e67-4e89-a205-d6eb19382b09","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"87f33c53-1a4c-420a-ad74-a158ce098b4c"}
