{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"Forbid`: The CronJob does not allow concurrent runs; if it is time for a new Job run and the previous Job run hasn't finished yet, the CronJob skips the new Job run. Also note that when the previous Job run finishes, `.spec.startingDeadline"}},"session_id":"b489fccf-1e67-4e89-a205-d6eb19382b09","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"f0037402-f8c8-4b1d-9641-8353a3fd1aa2"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"Seconds` is still taken into account and may result in a new Job run.\n- `Replace`: If it is time for a new Job run and the previous Job run hasn't finished yet, the CronJob replaces the currently running Job run with a new Job run\n\n##"}},"session_id":"b489fccf-1e67-4e89-a205-d6eb19382b09","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"55a1c625-c559-45ce-921c-2959fc2693c7"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" Jobs history limits\n\nThe `.spec.successfulJobsHistoryLimit` and `.spec.failedJobsHistoryLimit` fields specify how many completed and failed Jobs should be kept. Both fields are optional.\n\n- `.spec.successfulJobsHistoryLim"}},"session_id":"b489fccf-1e67-4e89-a205-d6eb19382b09","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"5533a70a-5e27-48b5-8150-068fa33b908f"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"it`: This field specifies the number of successful finished jobs to keep. The default value is `3`. Setting this field to `0` will not keep any successful jobs.\n- `.spec.failedJobsHistoryLimit`: This field specifies the number of failed finished job"}},"session_id":"b489fccf-1e67-4e89-a205-d6eb19382b09","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"0612ca7f-c775-47a9-912f-73cf110a8120"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"s to keep. The default value is `1`. Setting this field to `0` will not keep any failed jobs.\n```\n\n### A6 · `k8s-docs-garbage-collection-2026-08-24.md` (new)\n\n```markdown\n---\nsource_url: \"https://kubernetes.io/docs/concep"}},"session_id":"b489fccf-1e67-4e89-a205-d6eb19382b09","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"11f933b8-e44a-4f05-bee4-2549796777c6"}
