{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"ered: [\"owner-reference\", \"cascading-deletion\", \"orphaning\", \"ownership-chain\", \"label-selector\"]\n---\n# Garbage Collection (kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/architecture/garbage-collection/)\n\nGarbage collection is a"}},"session_id":"b489fccf-1e67-4e89-a205-d6eb19382b09","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"9204c6fc-9a68-416a-9a76-cddc1a57731d"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" collective term for the various mechanisms Kubernetes uses to clean up cluster resources. This allows the clean up of resources like the following:\n\n- Terminated pods\n- Completed Jobs\n- Objects without owner"}},"session_id":"b489fccf-1e67-4e89-a205-d6eb19382b09","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"c6d346f6-7706-4bbc-b547-a115c2a966bf"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" references\n- Unused containers and container images\n- Dynamically provisioned PersistentVolumes with a StorageClass reclaim policy of Delete\n- Stale or expired CertificateSigningRequests (CSRs)\n- Nodes deleted in the following"}},"session_id":"b489fccf-1e67-4e89-a205-d6eb19382b09","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"dfa6dfac-649b-4658-9b8b-b3e65e520918"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" scenarios: on a cloud when the cluster uses a cloud controller manager; on-premises when the cluster uses an addon similar to a cloud controller manager\n- Node Lease objects\n\n## Owners and d"}},"session_id":"b489fccf-1e67-4e89-a205-d6eb19382b09","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"30dc6282-904e-4bcb-85b6-6f9a2e7ee3fa"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"ependents\n\nMany objects in Kubernetes link to each other through *owner references*. Owner references tell the control plane which objects are dependent on others. Kubernetes uses owner references to give the control plane, and other API clients, the opportunity to clean up"}},"session_id":"b489fccf-1e67-4e89-a205-d6eb19382b09","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"c66800a2-d4cb-489e-b044-afa2ef0e7a1b"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" related resources before deleting an object. In most cases, Kubernetes manages owner references automatically.\n\nOwnership is different from the labels and selectors mechanism that some resources also use. For example, consider a Service that creates `EndpointSlice` objects. The"}},"session_id":"b489fccf-1e67-4e89-a205-d6eb19382b09","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"097102be-f2ee-4f3b-8ff5-63a0371ae5c8"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" Service uses *labels* to allow the control plane to determine which `EndpointSlice` objects are used for that Service. In addition to the labels, each `EndpointSlice` that is managed on behalf of a Service has an owner reference. Owner references help different parts of Kubernet"}},"session_id":"b489fccf-1e67-4e89-a205-d6eb19382b09","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"5ba53e13-1b0a-4563-a239-01ef99711a1a"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"es avoid interfering with objects they don't control.\n\nNote: Cross-namespace owner references are disallowed by design. Namespaced dependents can specify cluster-scoped or namespaced owners. A namespaced owner **must** exist in the same namespace as the dependent."}},"session_id":"b489fccf-1e67-4e89-a205-d6eb19382b09","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"f1249071-fab7-478e-b2f8-79d71fabd0e1"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" If it does not, the owner reference is treated as absent, and the dependent is subject to deletion once all owners are verified absent.\n\nCluster-scoped dependents can only specify cluster-scoped owners. In v1.20+, if a cluster-scoped depend"}},"session_id":"b489fccf-1e67-4e89-a205-d6eb19382b09","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"1521cb7c-9b99-445f-9655-7e350c56dd71"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"ent specifies a namespaced kind as an owner, it is treated as having an unresolvable owner reference, and is not able to be garbage collected.\n\nIn v1.20+, if the garbage collector detects an invalid cross-namespace `ownerReference`"}},"session_id":"b489fccf-1e67-4e89-a205-d6eb19382b09","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"16dd0299-61fb-49d9-a939-c248014bf90a"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":", or a cluster-scoped dependent with an `ownerReference` referencing a namespaced kind, a warning Event with a reason of `OwnerRefInvalidNamespace` and an `involvedObject` of the invalid dependent is reported."}},"session_id":"b489fccf-1e67-4e89-a205-d6eb19382b09","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"9a04a3b0-64d0-4ace-b69b-4958a63b27d5"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"\n\n## Cascading deletion\n\nKubernetes checks for and deletes objects that no longer have owner references, like the pods left behind when you delete a ReplicaSet. When you delete an object, you can control whether Kubernetes deletes"}},"session_id":"b489fccf-1e67-4e89-a205-d6eb19382b09","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"cceda833-5d5b-443e-aa79-0a8aace0862b"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" the object's dependents automatically, in a process called *cascading deletion*. There are two types of cascading deletion, as follows:\n\n- Foreground cascading deletion\n- Background cascading deletion\n\nYou can also control how and when garbage collection deletes resources that have owner references using Kubern"}},"session_id":"b489fccf-1e67-4e89-a205-d6eb19382b09","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"fd1a359c-6b76-4efc-a78e-4759c975769a"}
